---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import LibraryAssessment from '../../components/LibraryAssessment.astro';
import ClaimTrace from '../../components/ClaimTrace.astro';
import {archive,sourceHref} from '../../lib/archive';
import {accessLevels,accessLabels,roleLabels,libraryCard,authorPaths,assessmentFor,draftAssessments,resolveLibraryTarget,unassessedCount} from '../../lib/research-library';
import '../../styles/research-library.css';
const cards=archive.sources.map(s=>libraryCard(s.id));
---
<Site title="Research Library & Evidence Explorer" active="Sources">
<header class="wrap page-head research-header"><p class="kicker">THE ORIGINAL REFERENCES · A CLEARER RESEARCH TRAIL</p><h1><span class="library-title-prefix">Sources</span>Research Library<br/>&amp; <em>Evidence Explorer</em></h1><p class="lead">The books are still here. So are the questions. Find an author, see how much has been examined, and follow a claim to the passage behind it.</p><p class="research-edition">128 original bibliographic records · {cards.filter(c=>c.assessment).length} scoped assessments · {unassessedCount} not newly assessed · {draftAssessments.length} draft passage examples</p><p class="fine">Private read-only research preview. Independent historical, community, language and rights review pending; public release not granted.</p><nav class="library-jumps" aria-label="Research library sections"><a href="#author-paths">Follow an author</a><a href="#claim-trace">Follow one claim</a><a href="#original-sources">Browse all 128 references</a><a href="#draft-passages">See inspected passage examples</a></nav></header>
<section class="wrap library-legend" aria-label="Three different research questions"><div><h3>Access</h3><p>A catalogue, an abstract and an inspected passage tell you different things. A reachable PDF does not mean a complete book has been read.</p></div><div><h3>Evidence</h3><p>An author’s interpretation, a recorded statement and corroboration of a historical event require different assessments. Access is not a verification seal.</p></div><div><h3>Permission</h3><p>Rights and consent are separate from historical accuracy. No complete book, scan, cover, sacred verse or private testimony is republished here.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="author-paths" aria-labelledby="authors-heading"><div class="library-section-heading"><p class="kicker">ORIGINAL KNOWLEDGE, DISTINCT INTELLECTUAL VOICES</p><h2 id="authors-heading">Four paths into the references.</h2><p>These works remain connected to the preserved knowledge base. Each assessment states its edition, scope and limits; none claims a full commercial-book audit.</p></div><div class="author-paths">{authorPaths.map(path=><article class="author-path"><p class="kicker">A READING PATH, NOT AN ENDORSEMENT</p><h3>{path.name}</h3><p>{path.scope}</p><ul>{path.ids.filter(id=>assessmentFor(id)).map(id=><li><a href={sourceHref(id)}>{assessmentFor(id)!.workTitle}</a><p class="fine">{assessmentFor(id)!.edition} · {accessLabels[assessmentFor(id)!.access]}</p></li>)}</ul></article>)}</div></section>
<ClaimTrace/>
<section class="wrap section" id="original-sources" aria-labelledby="records-heading"><div class="library-section-heading"><p class="kicker">THE PRESERVED BIBLIOGRAPHY</p><h2 id="records-heading">128 original records. Still in order.</h2><p>Original titles, institutions, source types and routes are retained. New access labels are separate editorial notes. An earlier source note does not silently become a new inspection.</p></div>
<form id="library-filters" class="library-filters" role="search" hidden><div class="library-filter-grid"><div><label for="library-query">Search title, author, subject or institution</label><input id="library-query" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try Ogundiran, Ifa, biography or textiles"/></div><div><label for="library-access">Recorded access level</label><select id="library-access"><option value="all">All access levels</option>{accessLevels.map(level=><option value={level}>{accessLabels[level]}</option>)}</select></div><div><label for="library-role">Source role</label><select id="library-role"><option value="all">All source roles</option>{Object.entries(roleLabels).map(([role,label])=><option value={role}>{label}</option>)}</select></div></div><button class="button secondary" type="reset">Clear filters</button><p class="fine">Filters apply to the original records and draft example cards below. Author paths and the guided comparison stay available.</p></form>
<p id="library-filter-status" class="library-filter-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Showing 128 original records and {draftAssessments.length} draft passage examples.</p><noscript><p>All records and their links are shown below. Search and filtering need JavaScript; author links and native evidence disclosures work without it.</p></noscript>
<div class="source-directory">{cards.map(c=><article id={`library-${c.id}`} data-library-entry data-library-key={c.key} data-library-access={c.access} data-library-role={c.role} data-library-register="canonical"><p class="kicker">{c.host}</p><h2><a href={c.href}>{c.title}</a></h2><p>{c.kind}</p><p class="access-chip">{accessLabels[c.access]}</p><p class="library-record-meta">{c.assessment?`${c.creator} · ${roleLabels[c.role]}`:'Original record retained · no new work-level assessment'}</p><p class="library-status-only">Historical claim verification and reproduction rights remain separate and unapproved.</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="draft-passages" aria-labelledby="draft-heading"><div class="library-section-heading"><p class="kicker">SEPARATE DRAFT REGISTERS</p><h2 id="draft-heading">A passage, not a whole-book claim.</h2><p>These examples come from the existing story registers. They are additional draft pointers, not new entries in the frozen 128-source catalogue or newly discovered evidence.</p></div>{draftAssessments.map(a=>{const source=resolveLibraryTarget(a.target);return <article class="draft-evidence-card" id={`draft-${a.target.sourceId}`} data-library-entry data-library-key={[a.creator,a.workTitle,a.role,a.note].join(' ')} data-library-access={a.access} data-library-role={a.role} data-library-register="draft"><p class="kicker">PRIOR DRAFT SOURCE REGISTER</p><h3>{a.workTitle}</h3><p>{a.creator} · {source.host}</p><p class="access-chip">{accessLabels[a.access]}</p><details><summary>Inspect the recorded passage and its limits</summary><LibraryAssessment assessment={a}/></details></article>;})}</section>
<aside class="wrap notice library-policy"><h2>Sources have boundaries.</h2><p>Samuel Johnson’s books, including <cite>The History of the Yorubas</cite>, are not admissible factual authorities for this project. An unchecked derivative retelling is not independent evidence. A citation in another author’s bibliography alone does not prove every argument depends on Johnson; inspect the actual claim’s evidence.</p><p>Cheryl Johnson-Odim is a different scholar. Named, consenting Yorùbá community perspectives remain research priorities; a practitioner’s book catalogue is not authenticated testimony, a universal lineage account or permission to reproduce sacred material.</p><a href="/about/">Read the existing editorial limits</a></aside>
</Site>
<script>
import {matchesLibrary} from '../../lib/library-filter';
const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#library-filters');
const query=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#library-query');
const access=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#library-access');
const role=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#library-role');
const status=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#library-filter-status');
const entries=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-library-entry]'));
function update(){
  if(!query||!access||!role||!status)return;
  let canonical=0,draft=0;
  for(const entry of entries){const found=matchesLibrary({key:entry.dataset.libraryKey??'',access:entry.dataset.libraryAccess??'not-assessed',role:entry.dataset.libraryRole??'not-assessed'},query.value,access.value,role.value);entry.hidden=!found;if(found){if(entry.dataset.libraryRegister==='canonical')canonical++;else draft++;}}
  status.textContent=canonical+draft?`Showing ${canonical} original records and ${draft} draft passage examples.`:'No records match these filters. Clear filters to see the full directory.';
}
if(form&&query&&access&&role&&status){form.hidden=false;form.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();update();});query.addEventListener('input',update);access.addEventListener('change',update);role.addEventListener('change',update);form.addEventListener('reset',event=>{event.preventDefault();query.value='';access.value='all';role.value='all';update();});}
</script>
